From 249aa0db4b1b7865d7e2be7ce5826fe3f353c259 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mgirom <84082110+mgirom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 09:10:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] cpca: --kv-codebook flag and context parameter; codebook
 bound to model identity; f16 codebooks; finite check

- llama_context_params.kv_codebook (appended, default NULL) -> llama_memory_params ->
  llama_kv_cache constructor (trailing defaulted parameter); the hybrid memory passes
  it through to its attention cache. LLAMA_KV_CODEBOOK remains as a fallback.
- The codebook GGUF may carry cpca.model_arch / model_name / n_layer / n_head_kv /
  head_dim; a mismatch refuses with the reason. Not cryptographic: it catches the
  wrong model, which is the realistic mistake.
- Codebook tensors may be f16 (halves the file); every value is checked finite.
- common: --kv-codebook FNAME (env LLAMA_ARG_KV_CODEBOOK).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
